# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# This is not a style preference. The scanners split their input on \n and the
# captured /proc tables in test/fixtures are read byte for byte, so a CRLF
# checkout on Windows would make the parsers, the fixtures, and CI disagree
# about what a fixture says. The git hooks are shell scripts, and those do not
# run at all with CRLF line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never rewritten, whatever the content detection decides.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
